#: ../../../index.md:7
msgid "The LLVM C Library"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../index.md:9
msgid ""
"LLVM-libc is a from-scratch implementation of the C standard library, built "
"as part of the LLVM project. It is designed to be **modular** (any piece can "
"be used independently), **multiplatform** (Linux, GPU, baremetal embedded, "
"UEFI, macOS, Windows), and written in modern C++ for correctness, "
"performance, and safety."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../index.md:15
msgid "The logo was drawn by Jordan Abrahams-Whitehead"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../index.md:17
msgid "What Works Today"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../index.md:19
msgid ""
"LLVM-libc is **actively used in production** for a targeted set of use "
"cases, though coverage is still growing and many programs that depend on the "
"full C standard library (regex, locale, wide-character I/O, etc.) will not "
"yet compile against it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../index.md:24
msgid ""
"**Static-linked Linux servers and containers** — used in production at "
"Google (servers and Pixel Buds) on x86-64 and AArch64."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../index.md:26
msgid ""
"**GPU compute (AMDGPU, NVPTX)** — libc functions available in GPU kernels "
"via LLVM's offloading runtime. {doc}`GPU docs <gpu/index>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../index.md:28
msgid ""
"**Baremetal embedded (ARM, RISC-V, AArch64)** — minimal footprint builds for "
"microcontrollers and custom hardware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../index.md:30
msgid ""
"**UEFI applications** — experimental support for firmware development. {doc}"
"`UEFI docs <uefi/index>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../index.md:32
msgid ""
"**LLVM ecosystem internals** — libc++ and the offloading runtime consume "
"LLVM-libc directly via {doc}`Hand-in-Hand <hand_in_hand>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../index.md:34
msgid ""
"**Toolchain integrations** — pieces of LLVM-libc are used in Android Bionic, "
"Fuchsia, Emscripten, and the ARM embedded toolchain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../index.md:37
msgid ""
"Coverage is still growing. See the {doc}`implementation status <headers/"
"index>` pages for per-header detail, and the {doc}`platform support "
"<platform_support>` page for OS/architecture coverage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../index.md:41
msgid "Getting Started"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../index.md:43
msgid ""
"If you are new to LLVM-libc, {doc}`getting_started` is the right first stop. "
"It covers cloning, building, testing, and verifying your installation in one "
"place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../index.md:47
msgid ""
"Want to use LLVM-libc *alongside* your system libc instead of replacing it? "
"See {doc}`overlay_mode`."
msgstr ""

